    },
    {
      "id": "RK6zhQSoGXhg2m_ZvKIpQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2912.965128290939,
      "y": 1737.6371235383099,
      "width": 1419.7388916015625,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7PV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 65017414,
      "version": 713,
      "versionNonce": 1277560583,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791273832078,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Tokeniser converts all the texts/strings into tokens (i.e. breaking entire sentence/paragraph into words)\n\nIndexing maintains inverted index that is a key value pair where keys will be all the tokens and values will be array of\nobjects where each object consists of docId, Term Frequency (TF), Doc Length (docLen).\n\nRanker sorts the IDs based on the BM25 score which is calculated based on per doc TF, corpus Inverse Document Frequency (IDF)\nand docLen (can consider implementing Semantic Search by adding Vectors and Approximate Near Neighbour (ANN index)).\n\n\nRedis is used for hot query caching and autocomplete using prefix matching, also maintain the Redis NX for avoiding Cache Stampede, Staggered\nJitters in TTL for avoiding Cache Avalanche, also can use cache miss captures with short TTL to avoid Cache Penetration.\n\nAll the data stores (i.e. Trie Store, Inverted Index Store, Document Store and Redis) need to have sharding using hash ring, consistent hashing\nfor adding new servers and shards as well as each server/shard will have its own read replica setup.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "Bmlp1XBY14KlrWK71uOa1",
      "originalText": "Tokeniser converts all the texts/strings into tokens (i.e. breaking entire sentence/paragraph into words)\n\nIndexing maintains inverted index that is a key value pair where keys will be all the tokens and values will be array of\nobjects where each object consists of docId, Term Frequency (TF), Doc Length (docLen).\n\nRanker sorts the IDs based on the BM25 score which is calculated based on per doc TF, corpus Inverse Document Frequency (IDF)\nand docLen (can consider implementing Semantic Search by adding Vectors and Approximate Near Neighbour (ANN index)).\n\n\nRedis is used for hot query caching and autocomplete using prefix matching, also maintain the Redis NX for avoiding Cache Stampede, Staggered Jitters in TTL for avoiding Cache Avalanche, also can use cache miss captures with short TTL to avoid Cache Penetration.\n\nAll the data stores (i.e. Trie Store, Inverted Index Store, Document Store and Redis) need to have sharding using hash ring, consistent hashing for adding new servers and shards as well as each server/shard will have its own read replica setup.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
